From e7d488bddf965b871ecc2416f35084968288127f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rations <ehqcar@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:50:10 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 09/20] server: Detach asyncs from a queue before terminating
 them in free_async_queue().

free_async_queue() terminated each async while it was still linked into
the queue, and only then cleared async->queue and dropped the queue's
reference. async_terminate() queues an APC_ASYNC_IO to the async's
thread; when that APC cannot be queued, queue_apc() fails, the APC is
released unexecuted, and thread_apc_destroy() completes the async through
async_set_result(). That function still saw async->queue set, so it
unlinked the async and released the queue's reference itself. Back in
free_async_queue() the same reference was released again: refcount
underflow, and wineserver aborts in release_object() on
"assert( obj->refcount )".

On Haiku the APC can never be delivered by signal: the client does not
report a Unix thread id (get_unix_tid() has no Haiku branch and returns
-1), so send_thread_signal() always fails and any thread not already in
an APC wait cannot be reached. services.exe hits this on every shutdown:
its svcctl listener thread has a pending FSCTL_PIPE_LISTEN when it
flushes and closes the pipe, pipe_server_destroy() frees the listen
queue, and wineserver aborts. Traced with "wineserver -f -d2" and a
debug_server report: close_handle -> release_object(pipe_server) ->
pipe_server_destroy -> free_async_queue -> release_object(async) with
refcount already 0. On Linux the same sequence delivers the APC with
SIGUSR1 and completes normally.

Because wineserver dies before its shutdown timer runs flush_registry(),
every registry change made since the last 30-second periodic save is
lost. "wine regedit file.reg" never persisted, which broke licence data
that lives in the registry (MachineGuid, per-plugin UUIDs), and each
crash orphaned the prefix's services.exe processes.

Clearing async->queue before async_terminate() makes async_set_result()
leave the list and the reference alone; free_async_queue() then drops
the queue's reference exactly once, as it did before when the APC was
delivered. The list itself is being torn down, so the entry needs no
unlinking. Not Haiku-specific; any failed APC delivery hits it. The
underlying Haiku limitation (no per-thread signals from wineserver) is
left as is.
---
 server/async.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/server/async.c b/server/async.c
index ae51b2f7..691b7984 100644
--- a/server/async.c
+++ b/server/async.c
@@ -277,8 +277,11 @@ void free_async_queue( struct async_queue *queue )
     {
         if (!async->completion) async->completion = fd_get_completion( async->fd, &async->comp_key );
         async->fd = NULL;
-        async_terminate( async, STATUS_HANDLES_CLOSED );
+        /* detach before terminating: if no APC can be queued, async_terminate()
+         * completes the async through async_set_result(), which would otherwise
+         * remove it from this queue and drop the queue's reference a second time */
         async->queue = NULL;
+        async_terminate( async, STATUS_HANDLES_CLOSED );
         release_object( &async->obj );
     }
 }
-- 
2.47.3


From 412153e4496d9da1b08a21664c1fd782a2d43317 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rations <ehqcar@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:03:38 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 10/20] ntdll, server: Deliver signals to specific threads on
 Haiku.

get_unix_tid() had no Haiku branch and returned -1, so the server could
never signal a single thread: queuing an APC to a thread that was not
waiting failed, the APC was destroyed, and the pending I/O completed with
STATUS_ALERTED. Named-pipe readers then saw ERROR_ALERTED (seen as WiX
Burn's engine and UI losing their pipe connection).

Haiku thread ids are system-wide, so report find_thread(NULL) and send
the signal with send_signal(), which returns a status instead of setting
errno.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c |  3 +++
 server/ptrace.c          | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
index d626ad11..cc7a52aa 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
@@ -71,6 +71,7 @@
 #endif
 #endif
 #ifdef __HAIKU__
+#include <OS.h>
 #define SIGIO SIGPOLL
 #endif
 
@@ -1549,6 +1550,8 @@ static int get_unix_tid(void)
     ret = lwpid;
 #elif defined(__DragonFly__)
     ret = lwp_gettid();
+#elif defined(__HAIKU__)
+    ret = find_thread( NULL );
 #endif
     return ret;
 }
diff --git a/server/ptrace.c b/server/ptrace.c
index 2e6d93b7..bda79d71 100644
--- a/server/ptrace.c
+++ b/server/ptrace.c
@@ -47,6 +47,17 @@
 # include <sys/uio.h>
 #endif
 #include <unistd.h>
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+#define kill_thread haiku_kill_thread
+#define resume_thread haiku_resume_thread
+#define set_thread_priority haiku_set_thread_priority
+#define suspend_thread haiku_suspend_thread
+#include <OS.h>
+#undef kill_thread
+#undef resume_thread
+#undef set_thread_priority
+#undef suspend_thread
+#endif
 
 #include "ntstatus.h"
 #include "winternl.h"
@@ -226,6 +237,12 @@ static inline int tkill( int tgid, int pid, int sig )
     return ret;
 #elif (defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined (__FreeBSD_kernel__)) && defined(HAVE_THR_KILL2)
     return thr_kill2( tgid, pid, sig );
+#elif defined(__HAIKU__)
+    /* thread ids are system-wide; send_signal() returns a status, not -1 and errno */
+    status_t ret = send_signal( pid, sig );
+    if (ret == B_OK) return 0;
+    errno = (ret == B_BAD_THREAD_ID) ? ESRCH : ret;
+    return -1;
 #else
     errno = ENOSYS;
     return -1;
-- 
2.47.3


From 73a992a849a5d5136361151c604db9a83668ff08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rations <ehqcar@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:12:19 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 11/20] winegcc: Do not link with -ldl on Haiku.

Haiku provides dlopen() and friends in libroot and ships no libdl, so
every Winelib link failed unless an empty libdl.a was put in place by
hand.
---
 tools/winegcc/winegcc.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/winegcc/winegcc.c b/tools/winegcc/winegcc.c
index ad509c18..eb83446b 100644
--- a/tools/winegcc/winegcc.c
+++ b/tools/winegcc/winegcc.c
@@ -1413,7 +1413,10 @@ static void build(struct strarray input_files, const char *output)
 
     if (!nostdlib && !is_pe)
     {
+#ifndef __HAIKU__
+	/* Haiku has the dl functions in libroot and no libdl */
 	strarray_add(&link_args, "-ldl");
+#endif
 	strarray_add(&link_args, "-lm");
 	strarray_add(&link_args, "-lc");
 #ifdef __HAIKU__
-- 
2.47.3


From a773fe62ee0594dba2849d7e90dc7523debb87bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rations <ehqcar@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:00:46 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 12/20] ntdll: Support WoW64 (32-bit code) on Haiku.

32-bit Windows code needs a 32-bit code selector and a per-thread %fs
segment whose base is the 32-bit TEB. Stock Haiku has neither an LDT nor
a way to keep a 32-bit FS across context switches and signals, so every
32-bit PE exited with "No LDT support on this platform".

This needs a Haiku kernel with per-team LDT support, which adds these
arch_thread_control() calls next to THREAD_SET_GS_BASE:
THREAD_SET_LDT_ENTRY, THREAD_SET_FS_BASE, THREAD_GET_FS_BASE and
THREAD_GET_GS_BASE. The constants get fallback definitions here because
the stock headers lack them. On a stock kernel the call fails with
B_BAD_HANDLER and 32-bit processes exit with a clear message; 64-bit
code is unaffected.

The model is FreeBSD's: cs32_sel is the GDT USER32_CODE_SELECTOR (0x1b),
fs32_sel stays 0 so each thread allocates an LDT entry, and the kernel
saves the FS selector in fpu_state (offset 486) on signal delivery.
- The context macros read CS, SS and FS from the signal context instead
  of constants, and the segment save/restore that was compiled out on
  Haiku is enabled again. restore_context only accepts cs32_sel or
  cs64_sel.
- The syscall dispatchers restore the 64-bit FS base on entry through a
  C helper (Haiku syscall numbers are not stable, so no raw syscall),
  and reload the 32-bit FS selector and SS on return, as on Linux and
  FreeBSD.
- The %gs fault fixup uses THREAD_GET/SET_GS_BASE.
- system.c reports no FSGSBASE: the kernel keeps CR4.FSGSBASE off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c | 123 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c        |   2 +
 2 files changed, 107 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
index 51159fcb..4b40607d 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -87,6 +87,19 @@ extern void _thread_set_tsd_base(uint64_t);
 extern status_t		_kern_generic_syscall(const char *subsystem, uint32 function,
                                               void *buffer, size_t bufferSize);
 #endif
+/* 32-bit code support; needs a kernel that provides these (the installed
+ * headers may predate them) */
+#ifndef THREAD_SET_LDT_ENTRY
+#define THREAD_SET_LDT_ENTRY	2
+#define THREAD_SET_FS_BASE		3
+#define THREAD_GET_FS_BASE		4
+#define THREAD_GET_GS_BASE		5
+struct thread_ldt_entry
+{
+    uint32 index;
+    uint32 descriptor[2];
+};
+#endif
 #endif
 
 #include "ntstatus.h"
@@ -355,15 +368,16 @@ static inline const WORD *SS_sig_ptr( const ucontext_t *context )
 #define R13_sig(context)     ((context)->uc_mcontext.r13)
 #define R14_sig(context)     ((context)->uc_mcontext.r14)
 #define R15_sig(context)     ((context)->uc_mcontext.r15)
-#define CS_sig(context)      cs64_sel
-#define FS_sig(context)      NULL
+#define CS_sig(context)      ((context)->uc_mcontext.fpu.fp_fxsave.cs)
+/* %fs is saved after trap_number by kernels with 32-bit code support */
+#define FS_sig(context)      (*(WORD *)((char *)&(context)->uc_mcontext.fpu.fp_fxsave + 486))
 #define GS_sig(context)      NULL
-#define SS_sig(context)      NULL
+#define SS_sig(context)      ((context)->uc_mcontext.fpu.fp_fxsave.ss)
 #define EFL_sig(context)     ((context)->uc_mcontext.rflags)
 #define RIP_sig(context)     ((context)->uc_mcontext.rip)
 #define RSP_sig(context)     ((context)->uc_mcontext.rsp)
-#define TRAP_sig(context)    TRAP_x86_PAGEFLT
-#define ERROR_sig(context)   0
+#define TRAP_sig(context)    ((context)->uc_mcontext.fpu.fp_fxsave.trap_number)
+#define ERROR_sig(context)   ((context)->uc_mcontext.fpu.fp_fxsave.error_code)
 #define FPU_sig(context)     ((XMM_SAVE_AREA32 *)&(context)->uc_mcontext.fpu)
 #define XState_sig(context)  NULL
 
@@ -758,11 +772,14 @@ static inline void set_sigcontext( const CONTEXT *context, ucontext_t *sigcontex
     R14_sig(sigcontext) = context->R14;
     R15_sig(sigcontext) = context->R15;
     RIP_sig(sigcontext) = context->Rip;
-#ifndef __HAIKU__
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+    /* older kernels restore %cs from the signal context unchecked */
+    CS_sig(sigcontext)  = (cs32_sel && context->SegCs == cs32_sel) ? cs32_sel : cs64_sel;
+#else
     CS_sig(sigcontext)  = context->SegCs;
+#endif
     FS_sig(sigcontext)  = context->SegFs;
     EFL_sig(sigcontext) = context->EFlags;
-#endif
 }
 
 
@@ -875,11 +892,9 @@ static void save_context( struct thread_data *data, struct xcontext *xcontext,
     context->R14    = R14_sig(sigcontext);
     context->R15    = R15_sig(sigcontext);
     context->Rip    = RIP_sig(sigcontext);
-#ifndef __HAIKU__
     context->SegCs  = CS_sig(sigcontext);
     context->SegFs  = FS_sig(sigcontext);
     context->EFlags = EFL_sig(sigcontext);
-#endif
     context->SegDs  = ds64_sel;
     context->SegEs  = ds64_sel;
     context->SegGs  = ds64_sel;
@@ -1521,9 +1536,7 @@ static void setup_raise_exception( struct thread_data *data, ucontext_t *sigcont
         context_init_xstate( &stack->context, NULL );
     }
 
-#ifndef __HAIKU__
     CS_sig(sigcontext)  = cs64_sel;
-#endif
     RIP_sig(sigcontext) = (ULONG_PTR)pKiUserExceptionDispatcher;
     RSP_sig(sigcontext) = (ULONG_PTR)stack;
     /* clear single-step, direction, and align check flag */
@@ -1684,7 +1697,7 @@ __ASM_GLOBAL_FUNC( call_user_mode_callback,
                    "1:\tmovq %rdi,%rsp\n\t"    /* user_rsp */
                    "movq 0x98(%r14),%rbp\n\t"  /* prev_frame->rbp */
                    "ldmxcsr 0xd8(%r14)\n\t"    /* prev_frame->xsave.MxCsr */
-#if defined(__linux__) || defined(__FreeBSD__)
+#if defined(__linux__) || defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__HAIKU__)
                    "movb $1,0x340(%r13)\n\t"   /* amd64_thread_data()->syscall_dispatch */
                    "movw 0x338(%r13),%ax\n"    /* amd64_thread_data()->fs */
                    "testw %ax,%ax\n\t"
@@ -1923,7 +1936,6 @@ static inline BOOL handle_interrupt( struct thread_data *data, ucontext_t *sigco
     case 0x2c:
         rec->ExceptionCode = STATUS_ASSERTION_FAILURE;
         break;
-#ifndef __HAIKU__
     case 0x2d:
         if (CS_sig(sigcontext) == cs64_sel)
         {
@@ -1944,7 +1956,6 @@ static inline BOOL handle_interrupt( struct thread_data *data, ucontext_t *sigco
         rec->NumberParameters = 1;
         rec->ExceptionInformation[0] = context->Rax;
         break;
-#endif
     default:
         return FALSE;
     }
@@ -2213,6 +2224,9 @@ static inline BOOL check_invalid_gsbase( struct thread_data *data, ucontext_t *u
     amd64_get_gsbase( (void**)&cur_gsbase );
 #elif defined(__NetBSD__)
     sysarch( X86_64_GET_GSBASE, &cur_gsbase );
+#elif defined(__HAIKU__)
+    if (_kern_generic_syscall( THREAD_SYSCALLS, THREAD_GET_GS_BASE, &cur_gsbase, sizeof(cur_gsbase) ))
+        return FALSE;  /* older kernel: cannot tell */
 #elif defined(__APPLE__)
     /* init_handler() has already reset GSBASE, we can't determine what it was before the signal */
 #endif
@@ -2274,6 +2288,8 @@ static inline BOOL check_invalid_gsbase( struct thread_data *data, ucontext_t *u
     amd64_set_gsbase( data->teb );
 #elif defined(__NetBSD__)
     sysarch( X86_64_SET_GSBASE, &data->teb );
+#elif defined(__HAIKU__)
+    _kern_generic_syscall( THREAD_SYSCALLS, THREAD_SET_GS_BASE, &data->teb, sizeof(data->teb) );
 #elif defined(__APPLE__)
     /* leave_handler() will set GSBASE to the TEB */
 #endif
@@ -2767,6 +2783,18 @@ void ldt_set_entry( WORD sel, LDT_ENTRY entry )
         perror("i386_set_ldt");
         exit(1);
     }
+#elif defined(__HAIKU__)
+    struct thread_ldt_entry ldt_entry = { .index = sel >> 3 };
+    status_t status;
+
+    memcpy( ldt_entry.descriptor, &entry, sizeof(entry) );
+    status = _kern_generic_syscall( THREAD_SYSCALLS, THREAD_SET_LDT_ENTRY, &ldt_entry, sizeof(ldt_entry) );
+    if (status == B_BAD_HANDLER)
+    {
+        fprintf( stderr, "No LDT support in this Haiku kernel\n" );
+        exit(1);
+    }
+    if (status != B_OK) ERR( "THREAD_SET_LDT_ENTRY %#x failed: %#x\n", sel, (int)status );
 #else
     fprintf( stderr, "No LDT support on this platform\n" );
     exit(1);
@@ -2911,6 +2939,8 @@ void signal_init_process( TEB *teb )
         cs32_sel = ldt_alloc_entry( ldt_make_cs32_entry() );
 #elif defined(__FreeBSD__)
         cs32_sel = GSEL(GUCODE32_SEL, SEL_UPL);
+#elif defined(__HAIKU__)
+        cs32_sel = 0x1b;  /* USER32_CODE_SELECTOR; %fs uses an LDT entry per thread */
 #endif
     }
 
@@ -3105,6 +3135,19 @@ __ASM_GLOBAL_FUNC( signal_start_thread,
                    "jmp " __ASM_LOCAL_LABEL("__wine_syscall_dispatcher_return") )
 
 
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+/* Called by the dispatchers when 32-bit code left its %fs loaded: give the Unix
+ * side the thread's TLS back. */
+extern void haiku_set_tls_fs(void);
+void haiku_set_tls_fs(void)
+{
+    static const uint64 base;  /* 0: the thread's TLS */
+
+    _kern_generic_syscall( THREAD_SYSCALLS, THREAD_SET_FS_BASE, (void *)&base, sizeof(base) );
+}
+#endif
+
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           __wine_syscall_dispatcher
  */
@@ -3234,6 +3277,24 @@ __ASM_GLOBAL_FUNC( __wine_syscall_dispatcher,
                    "popq %r8\n\t"
                    "leaq -0x98(%rbp),%rcx\n"
                    "2:\n\t"
+#elif defined(__HAIKU__)
+                   "movw %fs,%si\n\t"
+                   "testw %si,%si\n\t"
+                   "jz 2f\n\t"
+                   "pushq %rcx\n\t"
+                   "pushq %rdx\n\t"
+                   "pushq %r8\n\t"
+                   "pushq %r9\n\t"
+                   "pushq %r10\n\t"
+                   "pushq %r11\n\t"
+                   "call " __ASM_NAME("haiku_set_tls_fs") "\n\t"
+                   "popq %r11\n\t"
+                   "popq %r10\n\t"
+                   "popq %r9\n\t"
+                   "popq %r8\n\t"
+                   "popq %rdx\n\t"
+                   "popq %rcx\n"
+                   "2:\n\t"
 #elif defined __APPLE__
                    "movq 0x320(%r13),%rdi\n\t"     /* amd64_thread_data()->pthread_teb */
                    "xorl %esi,%esi\n\t"
@@ -3280,15 +3341,19 @@ __ASM_GLOBAL_FUNC( __wine_syscall_dispatcher,
                    __ASM_CFI(".cfi_remember_state\n\t")
                    __ASM_CFI_CFA_IS_AT2(rcx, 0xa8, 0x01) /* frame->syscall_cfa */
                    "leaq 0x70(%rcx),%rsp\n\t"      /* %rsp > frame means no longer inside syscall */
-#if defined(__linux__) || defined(__FreeBSD__)
+#if defined(__linux__) || defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__HAIKU__)
                    "movb $1,0x340(%r13)\n\t"       /* amd64_thread_data()->syscall_dispatch */
                    "movw 0x338(%r13),%dx\n"        /* amd64_thread_data()->fs */
                    "testw %dx,%dx\n\t"
                    "jz 1f\n\t"
                    "movw %dx,%fs\n"
-# ifdef __FreeBSD__
+# if defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__HAIKU__)
                    /* reset %ss (after sysret) for AMD */
+#  ifdef __FreeBSD__
                    "movw $0x3b,%dx\n\t"           /* GSEL(GUDATA_SEL, SEL_UPL) */
+#  else
+                   "movw $0x23,%dx\n\t"           /* USER_DATA_SELECTOR */
+#  endif
                    "movw %dx,%ss\n\t"
 # endif
                    "1:\n\t"
@@ -3550,6 +3615,24 @@ __ASM_GLOBAL_FUNC( __wine_unix_call_dispatcher,
                    "popq %r9\n\t"
                    "popq %r8\n\t"
                    "2:\n\t"
+#elif defined(__HAIKU__)
+                   "movw %fs,%si\n\t"
+                   "testw %si,%si\n\t"
+                   "jz 2f\n\t"
+                   "pushq %rcx\n\t"
+                   "pushq %rdx\n\t"
+                   "pushq %r8\n\t"
+                   "pushq %r9\n\t"
+                   "pushq %r10\n\t"
+                   "pushq %r11\n\t"
+                   "call " __ASM_NAME("haiku_set_tls_fs") "\n\t"
+                   "popq %r11\n\t"
+                   "popq %r10\n\t"
+                   "popq %r9\n\t"
+                   "popq %r8\n\t"
+                   "popq %rdx\n\t"
+                   "popq %rcx\n"
+                   "2:\n\t"
 #elif defined __APPLE__
                    "movq 0x320(%r13),%rdi\n\t"     /* amd64_thread_data()->pthread_teb */
                    "xorl %esi,%esi\n\t"
@@ -3576,15 +3659,19 @@ __ASM_GLOBAL_FUNC( __wine_unix_call_dispatcher,
                    /* switch to user stack */
                    "movq 0x88(%rcx),%rsp\n\t"
                    __ASM_CFI(".cfi_restore_state\n\t")
-#if defined(__linux__) || defined(__FreeBSD__)
+#if defined(__linux__) || defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__HAIKU__)
                    "movb $1,0x340(%r13)\n\t"       /* amd64_thread_data()->syscall_dispatch */
                    "movw 0x338(%r13),%dx\n"        /* amd64_thread_data()->fs */
                    "testw %dx,%dx\n\t"
                    "jz 1f\n\t"
                    "movw %dx,%fs\n"
-# ifdef __FreeBSD__
+# if defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__HAIKU__)
                    /* reset %ss (after sysret) for AMD */
+#  ifdef __FreeBSD__
                    "movw $0x3b,%dx\n\t"           /* GSEL(GUDATA_SEL, SEL_UPL) */
+#  else
+                   "movw $0x23,%dx\n\t"           /* USER_DATA_SELECTOR */
+#  endif
                    "movw %dx,%ss\n\t"
 # endif
                    "1:\n\t"
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
index 7ecb8b4c..6fc66d4a 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
@@ -590,6 +590,8 @@ void init_shared_data_cpuinfo( KUSER_SHARED_DATA *data )
         features[PF_MOVDIR64B_INSTRUCTION_AVAILABLE]= !!(regs[2] & (1 << 28));
 #if defined(__linux__)
         features[PF_RDWRFSGSBASE_AVAILABLE] &= !!(getauxval( AT_HWCAP2 ) & 2);
+#elif defined(__HAIKU__)
+        features[PF_RDWRFSGSBASE_AVAILABLE] = FALSE;  /* the kernel does not enable it */
 #endif
     }
 
-- 
2.47.3


From 157be3a9d4c30c5b1add38cf58158bab7c4df2de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rations <ehqcar@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:00:46 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 13/20] ntdll, server: Use the xattr functions from libgnu on
 Haiku.

The Haiku port disabled HAVE_SYS_XATTR_H in ntdll and the server. Wine
stores reparse points (Windows symbolic links) and DOS attributes in
extended attributes, so FSCTL_SET_REPARSE_POINT failed with ENOSYS. Wine
Mono's installer creates symlinks in its CREATELINKS64 action and failed
with 1603, so every .NET custom action (WiX DTF) failed after it, for
example in the iLok License Support installer (0x80070643).

Haiku provides fgetxattr() and friends in libgnu, which maps them to BFS
attributes. Check for the library in configure and link ntdll and the
server with it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 configure.ac           | 2 ++
 dlls/ntdll/Makefile.in | 2 +-
 dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c | 5 -----
 server/Makefile.in     | 2 +-
 server/fd.c            | 1 -
 5 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index f7413e8e..342b2182 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -948,6 +948,8 @@ then
         [AC_COMPILE_IFELSE([AC_LANG_PROGRAM([[#include <sys/xattr.h>]], [[getxattr("", "", "", 0, 0, 0);]])],
                            [wine_cv_xattr_extra_args=yes],[wine_cv_xattr_extra_args=no])])
     test $wine_cv_xattr_extra_args != yes || AC_DEFINE(XATTR_ADDITIONAL_OPTIONS, 1, [Define if xattr functions take additional arguments (macOS)])
+    dnl Haiku provides the xattr functions in libgnu
+    AC_CHECK_FUNC(fgetxattr,,[AC_CHECK_LIB(gnu,fgetxattr,[AC_SUBST(XATTR_LIBS,"-lgnu")])])
 fi
 
 dnl **** Check for working dll ****
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/Makefile.in b/dlls/ntdll/Makefile.in
index 4c43b771..471a7f3e 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/Makefile.in
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@ IMPORTLIB = ntdll
 IMPORTS   = $(SYMCRYPT_PE_LIBS) $(ZLIB_PE_LIBS) $(MUSL_PE_LIBS)
 EXTRAINCL = $(SYMCRYPT_PE_CFLAGS) $(ZLIB_PE_CFLAGS)
 UNIX_CFLAGS  = $(HWLOC_CFLAGS)
-UNIX_LIBS    = $(IOKIT_LIBS) $(COREFOUNDATION_LIBS) $(CORESERVICES_LIBS) $(RT_LIBS) $(PTHREAD_LIBS) $(I386_LIBS) $(PROCSTAT_LIBS) $(HWLOC_LIBS)
+UNIX_LIBS    = $(IOKIT_LIBS) $(COREFOUNDATION_LIBS) $(CORESERVICES_LIBS) $(RT_LIBS) $(PTHREAD_LIBS) $(I386_LIBS) $(PROCSTAT_LIBS) $(HWLOC_LIBS) $(XATTR_LIBS)
 
 EXTRADLLFLAGS = -nodefaultlibs
 i386_EXTRADLLFLAGS = -Wl,--image-base,0x7bc00000
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
index 5bd392ae..66933910 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
@@ -165,11 +165,6 @@ typedef struct
 
 #endif  /* linux */
 
-#ifdef __HAIKU__
-//#include <sys/xattr.h>
-#undef HAVE_SYS_XATTR_H
-#endif
-
 #define IS_SEPARATOR(ch)   ((ch) == '\\' || (ch) == '/')
 
 #define INVALID_NT_CHARS   '*','?','<','>','|','"'
diff --git a/server/Makefile.in b/server/Makefile.in
index 0dd53951..e6cd264a 100644
--- a/server/Makefile.in
+++ b/server/Makefile.in
@@ -52,6 +52,6 @@ SOURCES = \
 	winstation.c
 
 UNIX_CFLAGS = $(INOTIFY_CFLAGS)
-UNIX_LIBS   = $(LDEXECFLAGS) $(RT_LIBS) $(INOTIFY_LIBS) $(PROCSTAT_LIBS)
+UNIX_LIBS   = $(LDEXECFLAGS) $(RT_LIBS) $(INOTIFY_LIBS) $(PROCSTAT_LIBS) $(XATTR_LIBS)
 
 unicode_EXTRADEFS = -DBINDIR="\"${bindir}\"" -DDATADIR="\"${datadir}\""
diff --git a/server/fd.c b/server/fd.c
index fa51e21f..4e275a5c 100644
--- a/server/fd.c
+++ b/server/fd.c
@@ -88,7 +88,6 @@
 #endif
 #ifdef __HAIKU__
 #undef ioctl
-#undef HAVE_SYS_XATTR_H
 #endif
 #ifdef HAVE_SYS_XATTR_H
 #include <sys/xattr.h>
-- 
2.47.3


From 75d0ad49d452239608c1f9d2c9981b4c9ceed440 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rations <ehqcar@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:27:35 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 14/20] ntdll, server: Support hardware breakpoints on Haiku.

Copy protection such as PACE (iLok) sets Dr0-Dr3 and Dr7 on its own
threads with SetThreadContext and expects EXCEPTION_SINGLE_STEP when a
breakpoint is hit. A probe that does not trap marks the process as
tampered, and the licence check fails later. The server's ptrace
get/set_thread_context are empty on Haiku, so the breakpoints were
never set.

This needs a Haiku kernel with THREAD_SET_DEBUG_REGISTERS, which sets the
calling thread's own breakpoints and reports DR6 in the signal context
(fpu_state offset 488, after the FS selector). The constant gets a
fallback definition because the stock headers lack it.
- The server no longer treats the debug registers as server-only
  (system_flags 0), so they travel with the context.
- Each thread loads its own: NtSetContextThread and
  set_thread_wow64_context on the thread itself, and restore_context and
  the thread start when another thread changed them while it was
  suspended.
- NtGetContextThread answers from the thread's own copy instead of a
  server call.
- trap_handler takes DR6 from the signal context, with the reserved bits
  set as Windows reports them (0xffff0ff0); PACE checks for them.

On a stock kernel the call fails, a warning is printed and the
breakpoints are ignored, as Windows ignores values it cannot use.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c | 115 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 server/thread.c                 |   6 ++
 2 files changed, 121 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
index 4b40607d..80cda84c 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -100,6 +100,15 @@ struct thread_ldt_entry
     uint32 descriptor[2];
 };
 #endif
+/* hardware breakpoints of a thread, with the same kernel support */
+#ifndef THREAD_SET_DEBUG_REGISTERS
+#define THREAD_SET_DEBUG_REGISTERS	6
+struct thread_debug_registers
+{
+    uint64 address[4];
+    uint64 dr7;
+};
+#endif
 #endif
 
 #include "ntstatus.h"
@@ -371,6 +380,8 @@ static inline const WORD *SS_sig_ptr( const ucontext_t *context )
 #define CS_sig(context)      ((context)->uc_mcontext.fpu.fp_fxsave.cs)
 /* %fs is saved after trap_number by kernels with 32-bit code support */
 #define FS_sig(context)      (*(WORD *)((char *)&(context)->uc_mcontext.fpu.fp_fxsave + 486))
+/* followed by DR6 of the last debug trap */
+#define DR6_sig(context)     (*(ULONG64 *)((char *)&(context)->uc_mcontext.fpu.fp_fxsave + 488))
 #define GS_sig(context)      NULL
 #define SS_sig(context)      ((context)->uc_mcontext.fpu.fp_fxsave.ss)
 #define EFL_sig(context)     ((context)->uc_mcontext.rflags)
@@ -863,6 +874,46 @@ static inline void leave_handler( struct thread_data *data, ucontext_t *sigconte
 }
 
 
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           set_haiku_debug_registers
+ *
+ * Load the current thread's debug registers through the kernel. The server
+ * cannot set them on Haiku: each thread does it for itself, also when it
+ * resumes after another thread changed its context.
+ */
+static void set_haiku_debug_registers( ULONG64 dr0, ULONG64 dr1, ULONG64 dr2, ULONG64 dr3,
+                                       ULONG64 dr7 )
+{
+    struct thread_debug_registers regs = { { dr0, dr1, dr2, dr3 }, dr7 };
+    status_t status = _kern_generic_syscall( THREAD_SYSCALLS, THREAD_SET_DEBUG_REGISTERS,
+                                             &regs, sizeof(regs) );
+
+    /* Windows ignores values it cannot use, too */
+    if (status != B_OK)
+        WARN_(seh)( "debug registers not set (Dr7 %#lx): %#x\n", (ULONG_PTR)dr7, (int)status );
+}
+
+
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           update_haiku_debug_registers
+ *
+ * Load the debug registers of a context the server handed back to the
+ * current thread, if another thread changed them.
+ */
+static void update_haiku_debug_registers( const struct amd64_thread_data *amd64_data,
+                                          const CONTEXT *context )
+{
+    if ((context->ContextFlags & CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS) != CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS) return;
+    if (amd64_data->dr0 == context->Dr0 && amd64_data->dr1 == context->Dr1 &&
+        amd64_data->dr2 == context->Dr2 && amd64_data->dr3 == context->Dr3 &&
+        amd64_data->dr7 == context->Dr7) return;
+    set_haiku_debug_registers( context->Dr0, context->Dr1, context->Dr2, context->Dr3,
+                               context->Dr7 );
+}
+#endif
+
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           save_context
  *
@@ -977,6 +1028,9 @@ static void restore_context( struct thread_data *data, const struct xcontext *xc
 
     if (amd64_data)
     {
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+        update_haiku_debug_registers( amd64_data, context );
+#endif
         amd64_data->dr0 = context->Dr0;
         amd64_data->dr1 = context->Dr1;
         amd64_data->dr2 = context->Dr2;
@@ -1070,6 +1124,10 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtSetContextThread( HANDLE handle, const CONTEXT *context )
         if (ret || !self) return ret;
         if (flags & CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS)
         {
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+            set_haiku_debug_registers( context->Dr0, context->Dr1, context->Dr2, context->Dr3,
+                                       context->Dr7 );
+#endif
             amd64_data->dr0 = context->Dr0;
             amd64_data->dr1 = context->Dr1;
             amd64_data->dr2 = context->Dr2;
@@ -1140,8 +1198,10 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtGetContextThread( HANDLE handle, CONTEXT *context )
 
     if (self && !frame) return STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED;
 
+#ifndef __HAIKU__  /* on Haiku the thread's own copy below is all there is */
     /* debug registers require a server call */
     if (needed_flags & CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS) self = FALSE;
+#endif
 
     if (!self)
     {
@@ -1256,12 +1316,23 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtGetContextThread( HANDLE handle, CONTEXT *context )
     /* update the cached version of the debug registers */
     if (needed_flags & CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS)
     {
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+        /* the server does not know them on Haiku: the cache is the thread's own copy */
+        context->Dr0 = amd64_data->dr0;
+        context->Dr1 = amd64_data->dr1;
+        context->Dr2 = amd64_data->dr2;
+        context->Dr3 = amd64_data->dr3;
+        context->Dr6 = amd64_data->dr6;
+        context->Dr7 = amd64_data->dr7;
+        context->ContextFlags |= CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS;
+#else
         amd64_data->dr0 = context->Dr0;
         amd64_data->dr1 = context->Dr1;
         amd64_data->dr2 = context->Dr2;
         amd64_data->dr3 = context->Dr3;
         amd64_data->dr6 = context->Dr6;
         amd64_data->dr7 = context->Dr7;
+#endif
     }
     set_context_exception_reporting_flags( &context->ContextFlags, CONTEXT_SERVICE_ACTIVE );
     return STATUS_SUCCESS;
@@ -1299,6 +1370,10 @@ NTSTATUS set_thread_wow64_context( HANDLE handle, const void *ctx, ULONG size )
         if (ret || !self) return ret;
         if (flags & CONTEXT_I386_DEBUG_REGISTERS)
         {
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+            set_haiku_debug_registers( context->Dr0, context->Dr1, context->Dr2, context->Dr3,
+                                       context->Dr7 );
+#endif
             amd64_data->dr0 = context->Dr0;
             amd64_data->dr1 = context->Dr1;
             amd64_data->dr2 = context->Dr2;
@@ -1401,12 +1476,23 @@ NTSTATUS get_thread_wow64_context( HANDLE handle, void *ctx, ULONG size )
         /* update the cached version of the debug registers */
         if (needed_flags & CONTEXT_I386_DEBUG_REGISTERS)
         {
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+            /* the server does not know them on Haiku: the cache is the thread's own copy */
+            context->Dr0 = amd64_data->dr0;
+            context->Dr1 = amd64_data->dr1;
+            context->Dr2 = amd64_data->dr2;
+            context->Dr3 = amd64_data->dr3;
+            context->Dr6 = amd64_data->dr6;
+            context->Dr7 = amd64_data->dr7;
+            context->ContextFlags |= CONTEXT_I386_DEBUG_REGISTERS;
+#else
             amd64_data->dr0 = context->Dr0;
             amd64_data->dr1 = context->Dr1;
             amd64_data->dr2 = context->Dr2;
             amd64_data->dr3 = context->Dr3;
             amd64_data->dr6 = context->Dr6;
             amd64_data->dr7 = context->Dr7;
+#endif
         }
         if (!(needed_flags & ~CONTEXT_I386_DEBUG_REGISTERS)) return ret;
     }
@@ -2474,11 +2560,20 @@ static void trap_handler( int signal, siginfo_t *siginfo, void *_sigcontext )
          * and only do a server call if there is any hw bp enabled. */
         if (!(context.c.EFlags & 0x100) || (context.c.Dr7 & 0xff))
         {
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+            /* save_context took Dr0-Dr3 and Dr7 from the thread's copy; the
+             * kernel reports in the signal context which breakpoints were hit.
+             * Windows passes DR6 as the processor reads it, with the reserved
+             * bits set, and copy protection checks for them. */
+            context.c.Dr6 = DR6_sig(sigcontext) | 0xffff0ff0;
+            amd64_thread_data( data )->dr6 = context.c.Dr6;
+#else
             /* (possible) hardware breakpoint, fetch the debug registers */
             DWORD saved_flags = context.c.ContextFlags;
             context.c.ContextFlags = CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS;
             NtGetContextThread(GetCurrentThread(), &context.c);
             context.c.ContextFlags |= saved_flags;  /* restore flags */
+#endif
         }
         context.c.EFlags &= ~0x100;  /* clear single-step flag */
         break;
@@ -2673,6 +2768,10 @@ static void usr1_handler( int signal, siginfo_t *siginfo, void *_sigcontext )
             frame->eflags = 0x200;
             fixup_frame_fpu_state( frame, sigcontext );
         }
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+        /* the server only knows the debug registers from the suspended context */
+        context->c.ContextFlags |= CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS;
+#endif
         NtGetContextThread( GetCurrentThread(), &context->c );
         if (xstate_extended_features)
         {
@@ -3070,6 +3169,22 @@ void init_syscall_frame( LPTHREAD_START_ROUTINE entry, void *arg, TEB *teb )
     }
 
     if (data->suspend) wait_suspend( &context );
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+    /* debug registers set by another thread while this one was suspended */
+    if (data->suspend)
+    {
+        update_haiku_debug_registers( thread_data, &context );
+        if ((context.ContextFlags & CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS) == CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS)
+        {
+            thread_data->dr0 = context.Dr0;
+            thread_data->dr1 = context.Dr1;
+            thread_data->dr2 = context.Dr2;
+            thread_data->dr3 = context.Dr3;
+            thread_data->dr6 = context.Dr6;
+            thread_data->dr7 = context.Dr7;
+        }
+    }
+#endif
 
     ctx = (CONTEXT *)((ULONG_PTR)context.Rsp & ~15) - 1;
     *ctx = context;
diff --git a/server/thread.c b/server/thread.c
index bb9728f6..4522128d 100644
--- a/server/thread.c
+++ b/server/thread.c
@@ -123,7 +123,13 @@ struct context
 #define CTX_WOW     1  /* context if thread is inside WoW */
 
 /* flags for registers that always need to be set from the server side */
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+/* none on Haiku: the debug registers travel with the context, and each
+ * thread loads its own through the kernel */
+static const unsigned int system_flags = 0;
+#else
 static const unsigned int system_flags = SERVER_CTX_DEBUG_REGISTERS;
+#endif
 
 static void context_dump( struct object *obj, int verbose );
 static struct object *context_get_sync( struct object *obj );
-- 
2.47.3


From cd9c940f4d4b3f557f0150b8ace372e33960a74c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rations <ehqcar@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:50:19 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 15/20] winerenku.drv: Add a native RenkuOS (Be API) graphics
 driver.

Every Wine port for Haiku-family systems draws through winewayland.drv,
and on RenkuOS Wayland is an in-process server that turns the protocol
back into BWindows and BBitmaps. This driver talks to the Be API
directly: each shown top-level HWND gets a BWindow, and win32u draws
child windows into the top-level window's surface as usual.

Layout follows winemac.drv: the Wine side is C (display.c, window.c,
surface.c, renku_main.c), the Be side is C++ (be_app.cpp, be_window.cpp),
and the two meet only in the plain-C header renku_be.h, because Wine's
internal headers and the Be headers cannot share a file.

- The BApplication starts lazily, on its own thread, the first time a
  screen or window is needed, so processes that never show a window
  never contact app_server. BScreen is only constructed after it runs:
  without be_app the screen is invalid.
- Be threads (the application looper and every BWindow looper) are
  spawned with Wine's asynchronous signals blocked, and restore the
  mask afterwards. Without that, the kernel may deliver SIGINT, SIGALRM
  or SIGUSR1 to a thread that has no TEB and Wine's handler faults on
  it; the sigprobe test (docs/probes in the port repo) shows both the
  fault without the block and that it is gone with it.
- UpdateDisplayDevices reports one GPU, and per BScreen a source, a
  monitor and the current mode. BScreen::SetToNext() returns an error
  on the last screen but leaves the BScreen valid, so the walk stops on
  the return value, not on IsValid().
- WS_CAPTION windows get B_TITLED_WINDOW_LOOK and GetWindowStyleMasks
  tells win32u that the decorator draws their caption and frame; all
  other windows are borderless and Wine paints them. A BWindow is only
  created once the window is shown, so hidden helper windows get none.
- Window surfaces are 32bpp top-down DIBs from window_surface_create();
  flush copies the dirty rows into a B_RGB32 BBitmap, whose byte order
  is the DIB's (B, G, R, X; "BGR-" in GraphicsDefs.h), and invalidates
  that rect in the view.
- Win32 threads only post messages to Be loopers (BMessenger blocks
  only when a port is full); a Be thread never waits on a Win32 thread.
  The driver's own mutex is never held across NtUser calls or surface
  creation and release, which can take win32u's locks.

configure builds the driver on Haiku when the Be headers are found and
fails with an error otherwise; --without-renku turns it off. It is never
built on other hosts.

Verified on RenkuOS (hrev60072+518) in a VM: notepad opens in a single
native titled window with its title, menu bar, a white edit area and a
blinking caret, drawn correctly; the display query reports the screen
(1024x768, 60 Hz). That window is black and white only, so the
red/blue channel order has not yet been seen on screen.

Not done yet: keyboard and mouse input, focus, and moving, resizing or
closing from the decorator (windows are created B_NOT_MOVABLE and
B_NOT_RESIZABLE until input exists); the work area does not leave out
the Deskbar; window shapes and layered windows; OpenGL; system
shutdown and Deskbar "Quit" requests are refused instead of becoming
WM_CLOSE. A fault on a Be thread runs Wine's SIGSEGV handler, which
does not return, so that thread freezes silently.
---
