2.47.3


From 84b937391b41629df8a351914f8431ad634291e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rations <ehqcar@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:52:17 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] winerenku.drv: OpenGL through OSMesa.

Mesa on RenkuOS has no DRI swrast module and no EGL platform Wine can
use (eglInitialize fails), so the driver had no OpenGL, and wined3d,
and with it every Direct3D program, could not create a device: plug-in
editors that draw with GL or D3D stayed blank. OSMesa does work: it
gives a windowless desktop GL 4.5 compatibility (or core) context on
llvmpipe, rendering into plain memory.

The GL half of opengl.c is the OSMesa backend that patch 8 of the
11.19 set put in winewayland.drv, moved here. It plugs into win32u
through struct opengl_driver_funcs only (WINE_OPENGL_DRIVER_VERSION 41,
as in 11.19), and sets no p_init_egl_platform, so win32u runs no EGL
setup; the port still configures --without-opengl, so win32u does not
load libEGL either. What carried over: WGL_TYPE_RGBA_ARB as the pixel
type (PFD_TYPE_RGBA is 0, which opengl32 reads as "no ARB attributes"
and then calls an entry point that is never set), contexts from
OSMesaCreateContextAttribs with 3.2 for an unversioned core request,
a 1x1 null surface for win32u's internal contexts, back buffers mapped
onto OSMesa's single front buffer, a resize that rebinds a current
context before the old buffer is freed, broken_sharing.

Presentation is new. The driver creates the client surfaces
(CreateClientSurface), and shows a GL window's frames in one of two
ways, chosen again on every update (win32u updates a client surface
when a window of its top-level moves, and before every present):
- A layer: a BView of its own in the top-level's BWindow, a child of
  the surface view, at the window's client area. A frame is copied
  into a BBitmap and posted to the view, and app_server shows it at
  once; app_server keeps the surface view's drawing out of it (no
  B_DRAW_ON_CHILDREN), and it passes the mouse to Wine like the
  surface view (the mouse code moved into a base class both share).
  Used when the window is shown in full: its top-level has a BWindow
  on screen, no DPI scaling applies, and its visible region is its
  whole client area, since a view would cover any Win32 window lying
  above it. This is what lets a plug-in editor's GL child window draw
  straight into its native window.
- Otherwise offscreen: win32u hands present() a DC on the window and
  the frame is drawn into it with GDI (StretchDIBits; OSMesa's BGRA
  with OSMESA_Y_UP 0 is a top-down 32-bpp DIB). GDI clips it and puts
  it in the top-level's window surface, which reaches the screen at
  its next flush: when a thread of the process waits for messages, or
  50 ms into continuous drawing (FLUSH_PERIOD, dlls/win32u/dibdrv/
  dc.c). winex11.drv draws every child GL window this way.
A layer keeps three BBitmaps and reuses one the view no longer holds.
If the looper is three frames behind, the newest frame goes into the
bitmap handed over last and is handed over again, so the last frame a
program draws is always the one left on screen. A front-buffer flush
(GL_FLUSH_PRESENT) presents like a swap.

configure: OSMesa is looked for independently of --with-opengl
(GL/osmesa.h, SONAME_LIBOSMESA), and its absence is an error unless
--without-osmesa is given, so the driver cannot silently build
without GL. The recipe needs devel:libosmesa (mesa_devel) to build and
lib:libosmesa (mesa) to run: libOSMesa is dlopen()ed, so haikuporter
cannot see it.

Verified from the work tree on the RenkuOS build VM (hrev60072+518,
Mesa 22.0.5), with programs built with mingw (docs/probes/glprobe.c,
d3dprobe.c in the port repository) whose expectations a native helper
(screencheck.cpp) checks against the screen itself, three runs each:
- GL 4.5 compatibility and 4.5 core contexts on llvmpipe;
- a top-level window's test pattern on screen the right way up and the
  right colours (a layer), about 1,200 to 1,500 clear-and-swap frames
  per second at 328x245, and the last frame of such a burst is the one
  left on screen;
- a GL child window on screen at its offset in its top-level (a
  layer), the top-level around it, clipped by the child, drawn with
  GDI;
- the child overlapped by a sibling window: drawn with GDI, the
  sibling stays on top; unclipped again, a layer again;
- a resized window renders at its new size;
- wined3d creates a D3D9 device and a D3D11 device (feature level
  11_0) with a swap chain, and their colours show on screen.
glprobe 29/29, d3dprobe 8/8.

Not verified: a real plug-in editor (needs vstbridge rebuilt on this
Wine); anything on bare metal; the mouse over a layer (it goes through
the same code as the surface view's, untested by hand); sharing
objects between core and compatibility contexts (hence
broken_sharing).
---
 configure.ac                     |   9 +
 dlls/winerenku.drv/Makefile.in   |   1 +
 dlls/winerenku.drv/be_window.cpp | 161 ++++++-
 dlls/winerenku.drv/opengl.c      | 786 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dlls/winerenku.drv/renku.h       |   6 +
 dlls/winerenku.drv/renku_be.h    |  17 +
 dlls/winerenku.drv/renku_main.c  |   2 +
 dlls/winerenku.drv/window.c      |  17 +
 8 files changed, 992 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 dlls/winerenku.drv/opengl.c

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index a33057e3..605684cb 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@ AC_ARG_WITH(netapi,    AS_HELP_STRING([--without-netapi],[do not use the Samba N
 AC_ARG_WITH(opencl,    AS_HELP_STRING([--without-opencl],[do not use OpenCL]),
             [if test "x$withval" = "xno"; then ac_cv_header_OpenCL_opencl_h=no; fi])
 AC_ARG_WITH(opengl,    AS_HELP_STRING([--without-opengl],[do not use OpenGL]))
+AC_ARG_WITH(osmesa,    AS_HELP_STRING([--without-osmesa],[do not use OSMesa (OpenGL in the RenkuOS driver)]))
 AC_ARG_WITH(oss,       AS_HELP_STRING([--without-oss],[do not use the OSS sound support]))
 AC_ARG_WITH(pcap,      AS_HELP_STRING([--without-pcap],[do not use the Packet Capture library]))
 AC_ARG_WITH(pcsclite,  AS_HELP_STRING([--without-pcsclite],[do not use PCSC lite]))
@@ -1504,6 +1505,14 @@ case $host_os in
     WINE_ERROR_WITH(renku,[test -z "$RENKU_LIBS"],
                     [Be API development files (Application.h) not found, the RenkuOS driver won't be supported.],
                     [enable_winerenku_drv])
+    dnl OpenGL in the RenkuOS driver is OSMesa's, dlopen()ed. Independent of --with-opengl, which
+    dnl looks for libEGL: there is no EGL platform Wine can use on RenkuOS.
+    if test "x$with_renku" != "xno" -a "x$with_osmesa" != "xno"
+    then
+        AC_CHECK_HEADER([GL/osmesa.h],[WINE_CHECK_SONAME(OSMesa,OSMesaGetProcAddress)])
+    fi
+    WINE_ERROR_WITH(osmesa,[test "x$with_renku" != "xno" -a -z "$ac_cv_lib_soname_OSMesa"],
+                    [OSMesa development files (GL/osmesa.h, libOSMesa) not found, the RenkuOS driver won't support OpenGL.])
     ;;
   *)
     enable_winerenku_drv=${enable_winerenku_drv:-no}
diff --git a/dlls/winerenku.drv/Makefile.in b/dlls/winerenku.drv/Makefile.in
index 7991a4cf..9177554c 100644
--- a/dlls/winerenku.drv/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/winerenku.drv/Makefile.in
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@ SOURCES = \
